.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-CERT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-cert
.Nd make or show an X.509 certificate for a key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis cert
.Fl k Ar key
.Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl e Ar email
.Op Fl -days Ar n
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Fl o Ar cert
.Op Fl -force
.Nm noqtis cert
.Fl k Ar key
.Fl -issuer Ar cert
.Fl -kem Ar kem.pub
.Op Fl -days Ar n
.Fl o Ar cert
.Op Fl -force
.Nm noqtis cert
.Fl -show Ar cert
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis cert
writes X.509 certificates (RFC 5280) for noqtis keys, as PEM, for
.Xr noqtis-smime 1
and for any other program that takes certificates.
.Pp
The first form writes a self-signed certificate for the signature key
.Ar key
(with
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub
beside it): ML-DSA (RFC 9881), SLH-DSA (RFC 9909) or Ed25519 (RFC
8410).
Its subject is the common name
.Ar name
and, with
.Fl e ,
the address
.Ar email
as the rfc822Name of its subjectAltName.
It signs mail and is a certification authority of path length 0, so
that it can issue the second kind.
A certificate nobody else signed proves nothing by itself: give it to
those who are to trust the key, over a channel that cannot be forged,
and they name it as their
.Fl -anchor .
.Pp
The second form writes a certificate for the ML-KEM public key
.Ar kem.pub
(RFC 9935), issued by
.Ar key
under the name and address of its own certificate
.Fl -issuer Ar cert :
the certificate others encrypt to.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
The secret signature key that signs the certificate.
.It Fl n Ar name , Fl -name Ns = Ns Ar name
The holder's name: 1 to 255 bytes of text.
.It Fl e Ar email , Fl -email Ns = Ns Ar email
The holder's address.
.It Fl -days Ar n
How long the certificate is valid, from five minutes ago: 1 to 36500
days.
Default: 730.
.It Fl -issuer Ar cert , Fl -kem Ar kem.pub
The second form: the certificate of
.Ar key ,
and the ML-KEM public key to certify.
.It Fl o Ar cert , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar cert
The certificate to write.
.It Fl -pass-fd Ar n , Fl -pass-env Ar name
The passphrase of a protected
.Ar key .
.It Fl -show Ar cert
Print what a certificate (PEM or DER) says: name, address, kind of key,
validity, and its fingerprint, the SHA-256 of the certificate.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing
.Ar cert .
.El
.Pp
The hybrid keys (ML-DSA with Ed25519) and HQC have no standard
certificate and get none.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 2 on a usage or file error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-DSA-65 -o me
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-KEM-768 -o me-kem
$ noqtis cert -k me -n "Ada Example" -e ada@example.org -o me.crt
$ noqtis cert -k me --issuer me.crt --kem me-kem.pub -o me-kem.crt
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-smime 1 ,
.Xr nqx5self 3
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 5280, RFC 9881, RFC 9909, RFC 9935.
